@host = http://localhost:5238

### Submit a batch (send it twice: the second call returns the same batch with 200, not a new one)
POST {{host}}/batches
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: batch-2026-10-07-001

{
  "payments": [
    {
      "reference": "INV-1001",
      "amount": "1250.50",
      "currency": "USD",
      "beneficiaryName": "Acme Supplies Ltd",
      "beneficiaryAccount": "GB29NWBK60161331926819",
      "bankPartner": "BANK-A"
    },
    {
      "reference": "INV-1002",
      "amount": "980",
      "currency": "EUR",
      "beneficiaryName": "Globex GmbH",
      "beneficiaryAccount": "DE89370400440532013000",
      "bankPartner": "BANK-B"
    }
  ]
}

### Invalid batch: every problem is reported, nothing is saved
POST {{host}}/batches
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: batch-2026-10-07-002

{
  "payments": [
    { "reference": "INV-1", "amount": "10.005", "currency": "USD", "beneficiaryName": "Acme", "beneficiaryAccount": "123", "bankPartner": "BANK-A" },
    { "reference": "INV-1", "amount": "5", "currency": "USX", "beneficiaryName": "", "beneficiaryAccount": "123", "bankPartner": "BANK-A" }
  ]
}

### Get a batch (paste the id from the first response)
GET {{host}}/batches/a2801ea9-3ca9-4254-9936-8508f678c3e3
